`element` declares its events, so codegen reads the declaration rather than
matching names: which listener is attached, whether it takes an event
argument, and what that argument stands for all come from there. @error
carries ErrorEvent, whose fields the element declares nothing of, so the
parameter stands for the event and the listener takes it. @input carries
InputEvent{value}, and `value` IS a prop of the element, so the field is the
control's own state, read back off the target. A handler that declares no
parameter gets no argument in the signature -- the body has nothing that could
resolve to the event. An event the element declares no payload for reaches its
own DOM event through the wildcard event and not click's listener, on the
static path and equally on the lowered one, where the element is built by JS
and the listener is attached inside the slot renderer.

Before, three name lists disagreed. An event outside click/input/change was
routed to a registration that binds no event parameter, and the emitted
signature was picked by a separate `event == "input" || event == "change"`
test -- so `@error(e) { msg = e.message }` compiled to a listener with no `e`
and the body threw ReferenceError. On the lowered (JS-built) path a fourth
list dropped any event outside click/input/change/submit on the floor.

deny out/none/html/index.html `addEventListener\("error", function\(\)` -- @error's handler reads the event, so an error listener with an empty parameter list is the old name-matched signature coming back

-- events.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:app"
import "sngl:platform/html"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component main {
    var msg string = ""
    var txt string = ""
    var hits int = 0
    var rows list<string> = ["a"]

    window {
        html.img(src="x.png", @error(e) { msg = e.message })
        html.input(@input(e) { txt = e.value })
        html.button(@click { hits = hits + 1 })
        html.div(@mouseover { hits = hits + 1 })
        for var r = rows {
            html.li(textContent=r, @mouseover { hits = hits + 1 })
        }
    }
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
